tour io-comments
kind layer
author ai
group map
note The io-comments crate's surface: the boundary between the domain Comments and the comment files. Callers (the CLI's comment commands, the GUI's comment handlers) make a CommentStore for a root, load, then write or remove one comment at a time; nothing batches or waits for a save. The store's directory is the VCS's shared directory plus codemap-comments (jj's .jj/repo, git's common dir), so every jj workspace and git worktree of one repository reads the same comments and no commit carries them; with neither VCS it is .codemap-comments under the root. One file per comment, named <id>.comment, so writing one comment never touches another and two sessions answering different comments never collide. The format is line-based key/value text with a version line first; text fields escape backslashes and newlines. Every fault comes back as a value naming the file and line.

